From 9b7fc3c67b01a54b079c03719f775a8fa990d3fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:52:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Park local Kanban/loop wakes for core updates;
 active-work publishes update_pausable on every unit

A Kanban notice (or /loop tick, plugin injection, heartbeat) on a local Desktop
route is admitted as local_automation_v1, and session_update_pause_ingress.
supported() refused every such admission, so the turn never bound an eligible
pause scope (update_pausable stayed false) and a restart-safe drain waited on it
for its whole claim lease (laptop-1 11-12 06:03 incident 13448, 07:16 incident
14995: chat f07c32).

supported() now admits a local-route producer wake: the claim re-checks its
route (check_local_automation) and resume_event keeps only its mute/heartbeat
traits, exactly as for a native notice. Still excluded: noted completions
(async delegation, process completion/watch, cron), which note_if_unviewed would
write as a note at an unviewed resume; detached-route wakes; API and malformed
descriptors.

The active-work verb now publishes update_pausable (e055b76f94's per-chat flag,
read from the installed hook) on every unit, False for api/delegation/managed/
cron, so a consumer can require `update_pausable is True` and never mistake a
missing field for a parkable unit.

Proof: RED on base 465e7d1fa1: kanban/loop/plugin eligibility rows, the
ingress table row, the composed local Kanban wake (park at the step boundary,
admission stays started, resumes as the same admission and completes), and the
verb test. GREEN: 48/48 across the touched files plus the update_pausable and
composed pause suites.
